---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'Bug Days gRPC Client',
    description: 'A browser-based gRPC API client with protobuf encoding, response streaming, metadata, authentication, history, saved requests, and a native gRPC bridge.',
    url: 'https://bugdays.com/grpc-client',
    applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any',
    isAccessibleForFree: true,
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
    featureList: [
      'Native gRPC through the Holy CORS local bridge',
      'Direct gRPC-Web requests',
      'Protocol Buffer encoding and decoding',
      'Unary and server-streaming RPCs',
      'Metadata and authentication',
      'Saved requests and local history'
    ]
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Can a browser call a native gRPC server?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Yes, with the optional Holy CORS local bridge. It translates browser-safe gRPC-Web framing into native HTTP/2 gRPC and returns trailers in a format the browser can read.' }
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Does this online gRPC client upload my proto file?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'No. Proto parsing, protobuf encoding, response decoding, saved requests, and history happen in your browser.' }
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Which gRPC calls are supported?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Unary and server-streaming calls are supported. Browser fetch APIs cannot provide the full bidirectional stream control needed for client-streaming and bidirectional gRPC calls.' }
      }
    ]
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Online gRPC Client — Native gRPC & gRPC-Web Tester"
  description="Test native gRPC and gRPC-Web APIs from your browser. Import .proto files, send protobuf requests, inspect messages, headers and trailers, and save request history locally."
  keywords="online gRPC client, gRPC tester, native gRPC client, gRPC web client, protobuf tester, proto file parser, gRPC request builder, server streaming gRPC, Postman for gRPC"
  breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Network Tools', href: '/network-tools' }, { name: 'gRPC Client' }]}
  toolId="grpc-client"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1500px] space-y-5">
    <header class="flex flex-col gap-3 xl:flex-row xl:items-end xl:justify-between">
      <div>
        <div class="mb-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
          <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-slate-100">gRPC Client</h1>
          <span class="rounded-full bg-indigo-100 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-700 dark:bg-indigo-950 dark:text-indigo-300">protobuf-native</span>
        </div>
        <p class="max-w-3xl text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">Import your contract, choose a method, and inspect real protobuf responses. Call gRPC-Web directly or let Holy CORS bridge the browser to a native HTTP/2 gRPC service.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <span class="text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">Local bridge</span>
        <span id="bridge-status" class="rounded-full bg-gray-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-gray-600 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300">Checking…</span>
        <button id="check-bridge-btn" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-3 py-1.5 font-medium hover:bg-gray-50 dark:border-slate-600 dark:hover:bg-slate-800">Check again</button>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section id="bridge-notice" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm text-amber-950 dark:border-amber-900 dark:bg-amber-950/30 dark:text-amber-100">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 lg:flex-row lg:items-center lg:justify-between">
        <div><strong>Start the local bridge to call native gRPC.</strong><span class="ml-1">It runs on your machine and connects this page to your HTTP/2 service.</span></div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <code class="rounded bg-white/80 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs dark:bg-slate-900">brew trust bugdays-com/tap && brew install bugdays-com/tap/holy-cors && holy-cors</code>
          <button id="copy-install-btn" class="rounded-lg bg-amber-900 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-white dark:bg-amber-200 dark:text-amber-950">Copy command</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white shadow-sm dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="grid gap-2 border-b border-gray-200 p-3 dark:border-slate-700 md:grid-cols-[175px_minmax(0,1fr)_auto]">
        <select id="transport" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white px-3 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:border-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100">
          <option value="native">Native gRPC (bridge)</option>
          <option value="direct">Direct gRPC-Web</option>
        </select>
        <input id="endpoint-url" data-share-key="endpoint" type="text" spellcheck="false" class="min-w-0 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white px-3 py-2.5 font-mono text-sm text-gray-900 dark:border-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100" placeholder="localhost:50051" />
        <div class="flex gap-2"><button id="cancel-btn" class="hidden rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold dark:border-slate-600">Cancel</button><button id="send-btn" class="rounded-lg bg-indigo-600 px-7 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-indigo-700 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50">Send</button></div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid min-h-[690px] xl:grid-cols-[310px_minmax(0,1fr)]">
        <aside class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-gray-50/70 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-950/40 xl:border-b-0 xl:border-r">
          <div class="border-b border-gray-200 p-3 dark:border-slate-700">
            <div class="mb-2 flex items-center justify-between"><h2 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">Contract</h2><button id="load-sample-btn" class="text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-600 hover:underline dark:text-indigo-400">Load sample</button></div>
            <label class="block cursor-pointer rounded-lg border border-dashed border-indigo-300 bg-indigo-50 px-3 py-2 text-center text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-700 hover:bg-indigo-100 dark:border-indigo-800 dark:bg-indigo-950/40 dark:text-indigo-300">Import .proto files<input id="proto-files" type="file" accept=".proto,text/plain" multiple class="hidden" /></label>
            <details class="mt-2">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">Or paste a definition</summary>
              <textarea id="proto-input" data-share-key="proto" class="mt-2 h-36 w-full resize-y rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white p-2 font-mono text-xs text-gray-900 dark:border-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100" placeholder='syntax = "proto3";'></textarea>
              <button id="parse-proto-btn" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-lg bg-slate-800 px-3 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-white dark:bg-slate-700">Parse definition</button>
            </details>
            <div id="contract-summary" class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">No contract loaded</div>
            <div id="proto-warnings" class="mt-2 hidden rounded bg-amber-50 p-2 text-xs text-amber-800 dark:bg-amber-950/40 dark:text-amber-200"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3">
            <input id="method-search" type="search" class="mb-3 w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-sm dark:border-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-900" placeholder="Filter methods…" />
            <div id="services-list" class="space-y-4 text-sm"><p class="rounded-lg border border-dashed border-gray-300 p-4 text-center text-xs text-gray-500 dark:border-slate-700 dark:text-slate-400">Load a .proto contract to discover services.</p></div>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <div class="min-w-0">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 border-b border-gray-200 px-4 py-3 dark:border-slate-700 lg:flex-row lg:items-center lg:justify-between">
            <div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2"><span id="method-type" class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-600 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300">No method</span><code id="selected-method" class="truncate text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-700 dark:text-indigo-300">Select a method</code></div><div id="method-signature" class="mt-1 truncate font-mono text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400"></div></div>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <button id="save-request-btn" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold dark:border-slate-600">Save</button>
              <button id="copy-grpcurl-btn" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold dark:border-slate-600">Copy grpcurl</button>
              <button id="export-btn" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold dark:border-slate-600">Export</button>
              <label class="cursor-pointer rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold dark:border-slate-600">Import<input id="import-state" type="file" accept="application/json,.json" class="hidden" /></label>
              <button class="share-trigger rounded-lg border border-indigo-300 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-700 dark:border-indigo-800 dark:text-indigo-300">Share</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid min-h-[630px] 2xl:grid-cols-2">
            <section class="min-w-0 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 2xl:border-b-0 2xl:border-r">
              <div class="flex border-b border-gray-200 px-3 dark:border-slate-700" data-tab-group="request">
                <button class="tab-btn border-b-2 border-indigo-600 px-3 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-600" data-tab="message">Message</button><button class="tab-btn border-b-2 border-transparent px-3 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500" data-tab="metadata">Metadata</button><button class="tab-btn border-b-2 border-transparent px-3 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500" data-tab="auth">Auth</button><button class="tab-btn border-b-2 border-transparent px-3 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500" data-tab="options">Options</button>
              </div>
              <div class="tab-panel p-4" data-tab-panel="request:message"><div class="mb-2 flex justify-between text-xs"><label for="request-json" class="font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-slate-200">Request JSON</label><button id="format-request-btn" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">Format</button></div><textarea id="request-json" data-share-key="request" spellcheck="false" class="h-[440px] w-full resize-y rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-slate-950 p-3 font-mono text-sm leading-6 text-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700" placeholder="{}"></textarea><div id="request-validation" class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">Request is encoded as Protocol Buffers in your browser.</div></div>
              <div class="tab-panel hidden p-4" data-tab-panel="request:metadata"><div id="metadata-list" class="space-y-2"></div><button id="add-metadata-btn" class="mt-3 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-3 py-2 text-xs font-semibold dark:border-slate-600">+ Add metadata</button><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">Custom metadata is included in saved requests. Sensitive standard headers are redacted from history and exports.</p></div>
              <div class="tab-panel hidden space-y-4 p-4" data-tab-panel="request:auth"><div><label class="mb-1 block text-xs font-semibold">Authentication</label><select id="auth-type" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white p-2 text-sm dark:border-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-800"><option value="none">No auth</option><option value="bearer">Bearer token</option><option value="basic">Basic auth</option></select></div><div id="bearer-fields" class="hidden"><label class="mb-1 block text-xs font-semibold">Token</label><input id="bearer-token" type="password" autocomplete="off" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white p-2 font-mono text-sm dark:border-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-800" placeholder="Not saved or shared" /></div><div id="basic-fields" class="hidden grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><input id="basic-user" autocomplete="off" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white p-2 text-sm dark:border-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-800" placeholder="Username" /><input id="basic-password" type="password" autocomplete="off" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white p-2 text-sm dark:border-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-800" placeholder="Password (not saved)" /></div><p class="text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">Credentials stay in this tab and are deliberately omitted from shares, exports, saved requests, and history.</p></div>
              <div class="tab-panel hidden space-y-4 p-4" data-tab-panel="request:options"><div><label class="mb-1 block text-xs font-semibold">Deadline (milliseconds)</label><input id="deadline-ms" type="number" min="1" max="99999999" value="30000" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white p-2 text-sm dark:border-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-800" /></div><div><label class="mb-1 block text-xs font-semibold">Holy CORS bridge URL</label><input id="bridge-url" value="http://127.0.0.1:2345" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-white p-2 font-mono text-sm dark:border-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-800" /></div><label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm"><input id="save-history" type="checkbox" checked /> Save non-secret request history in this browser</label></div>
            </section>

            <section class="min-w-0">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-gray-200 px-4 dark:border-slate-700"><div class="flex" data-tab-group="response"><button class="tab-btn border-b-2 border-indigo-600 px-3 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-600" data-tab="messages">Messages <span id="message-count"></span></button><button class="tab-btn border-b-2 border-transparent px-3 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500" data-tab="headers">Headers</button><button class="tab-btn border-b-2 border-transparent px-3 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500" data-tab="trailers">Trailers</button><button class="tab-btn border-b-2 border-transparent px-3 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500" data-tab="raw">Raw</button></div><div class="flex gap-2"><button id="copy-response-btn" class="text-xs text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">Copy</button><button id="download-response-btn" class="text-xs text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">Download</button></div></div>
              <div class="flex min-h-[45px] flex-wrap items-center gap-3 border-b border-gray-100 px-4 py-2 text-xs dark:border-slate-800"><span id="status-badge" class="rounded-full bg-gray-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-gray-600 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300">Not sent</span><span id="response-time" class="text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400"></span><span id="response-size" class="text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400"></span></div>
              <div id="response-empty" class="flex h-[475px] items-center justify-center p-8 text-center text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400"><div><div class="mb-2 text-3xl">⇄</div>Select a method and send a request.<br />Decoded messages, metadata, status and trailers appear here.</div></div>
              <div class="tab-panel hidden p-4" data-tab-panel="response:messages"><pre id="response-messages" class="h-[445px] overflow-auto whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-lg bg-slate-950 p-3 font-mono text-sm leading-6 text-slate-100"></pre></div>
              <div class="tab-panel hidden p-4" data-tab-panel="response:headers"><pre id="response-headers" class="h-[445px] overflow-auto whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-lg bg-slate-950 p-3 font-mono text-xs leading-5 text-slate-100"></pre></div>
              <div class="tab-panel hidden p-4" data-tab-panel="response:trailers"><pre id="response-trailers" class="h-[445px] overflow-auto whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-lg bg-slate-950 p-3 font-mono text-xs leading-5 text-slate-100"></pre></div>
              <div class="tab-panel hidden p-4" data-tab-panel="response:raw"><pre id="response-raw" class="h-[445px] overflow-auto whitespace-pre-wrap break-all rounded-lg bg-slate-950 p-3 font-mono text-xs leading-5 text-slate-100"></pre></div>
            </section>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div id="error-box" role="alert" class="hidden whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-4 text-sm text-red-800 dark:border-red-900 dark:bg-red-950/40 dark:text-red-200"></div>
    <section class="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900"><div class="mb-3 flex items-center justify-between"><h2 class="font-semibold">Saved requests</h2><button id="clear-saved-btn" class="text-xs text-gray-500">Clear</button></div><div id="saved-list" class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">Nothing saved yet.</div></div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900"><div class="mb-3 flex items-center justify-between"><h2 class="font-semibold">Local history</h2><button id="clear-history-btn" class="text-xs text-gray-500">Clear</button></div><div id="history-list" class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">No requests yet.</div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="rounded-xl border border-indigo-200 bg-indigo-50 p-5 dark:border-indigo-900 dark:bg-indigo-950/30">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-slate-100">Native gRPC without an Envoy configuration</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-sm leading-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-slate-300">Browsers cannot expose the HTTP/2 controls and trailing metadata required by native gRPC. Holy CORS fills that narrow gap locally: the page creates a real protobuf request, the bridge sends it as native gRPC over HTTP/2, and response trailers are translated back for inspection here.</p>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-3 text-sm"><div class="rounded-lg bg-white p-3 dark:bg-slate-900"><strong>1. Install once</strong><code class="mt-2 block text-xs">brew trust bugdays-com/tap<br />brew install bugdays-com/tap/holy-cors</code></div><div class="rounded-lg bg-white p-3 dark:bg-slate-900"><strong>2. Run locally</strong><code class="mt-2 block text-xs">holy-cors</code></div><div class="rounded-lg bg-white p-3 dark:bg-slate-900"><strong>3. Send</strong><p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">The status badge turns green when the bridge is ready.</p></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="space-y-5 py-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      <div><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-slate-100">A practical online gRPC client</h2><p class="mt-2 max-w-5xl leading-7">This client parses real Protocol Buffer definitions rather than guessing at fields with regular expressions. It validates JSON against the selected request type, serializes protobuf bytes, frames a gRPC-Web request, incrementally decodes streamed response frames, and displays gRPC status and trailing metadata separately.</p></div>
      <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3"><div><h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-slate-100">Contract-aware requests</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6">Load multiple imported proto files, browse services, generate request templates, and catch type errors before sending.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-slate-100">Useful debugging context</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6">Inspect decoded messages, HTTP headers, gRPC trailers, status codes, elapsed time, and raw response bytes.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-slate-100">Local by design</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6">Proto parsing and saved history stay in the browser. Authentication secrets are excluded from saved requests, history, shares, and exports.</p></div></div>
      <details class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-700"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-slate-100">Streaming support and browser limits</summary><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6">Unary and server-streaming RPCs work in binary mode. Client-streaming and bidirectional-streaming methods remain visible for contract exploration, but Send is disabled because the browser Fetch API does not provide portable full-duplex request streaming. Use grpcurl or a native SDK for those calls.</p></details>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  import { initGrpcClient } from '../lib/grpc-client-app';
  initGrpcClient();
</script>
